  "summary": "Murphy's single 60-minute Shakti session 'to try to create an intense experience in ONE session', with his hippocampal 'LTP' signal over both temporal lobes on the 8 Coil Shakti, switching between the two coil pairs after each signal (the vendor's standard mode). The vendor's file is not published; the primed burst played here is rebuilt from published descriptions of the signal.",
  "setting": "Blindfold, earplugs or a sound-blocking headset (the vendor: 'substituting white noise won't work'), no interruptions and no plans afterwards. Murphy: 'For the first twenty minutes, not much happens.'",
  "schedule": "A one-off for a single intense experience, not a series (the vendor: repeating it 'might eventually elicit an unpleasant experience'); at most once every 3 weeks.",
  "notes": "The vendor describes a one-off 60-minute session that 'should be bilateral'; its standard, slow mode switches stereo channels 'after one instance of the signal' (pages on 60-minute sessions and the 8 Coil Shakti). It identifies its hippocampal 'LTP' signal with that of Persinger, Richards & Koren 1994, a 2-ms pulse followed 150 ms later by four 2-ms pulses (p.2 [192]); Tsang 2004 describes the Shakti's signal as 'one pulse followed 170 ms later by four high frequency pulses about 3.8 times per sec', once every 4.76 s (p.5 [1017]). Four coils sit over each temporal lobe: top C5/C6 with bottom T9/T10 as one pair per side, front FT7/FT8 with back TP7/TP8 as the other. One train plays on the first pair, the next about 4.74 s later on the second; each pair gets a train about every 9.5 s. The hippocampal signal is the primed burst: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]). It is rebuilt from descriptions: the vendor's file is not published. Each pair has one (+) and one (-) coil after the vendor's 'Getting started' chart; its photos give other signs. Site names are the project's reading. Field strength: the vendor's 10 to 50 mG are gaussmeter readings at a coil (FAQ). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. At 1 uT that is about 56 uT at the coil face, 11 to 56 times the vendor's level. Support: the vendor's claims only. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). For the vendor, anxiety or fear usually shows that a hippocampal session 'has gone on too long': stop then. With headache or pressure (about 2% with hippocampal signals), lower the intensity by one third. Not for people with epilepsy, seizure history or a psychiatric condition; stop on distress.",
  "targets": ["left-hippocampus-head", "left-hippocampus-body", "left-hippocampus-tail", "right-hippocampus-head", "right-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-tail"],
